# Line endings: LF, deliberately.
#
# This app deploys to Linux, so LF is what actually runs. git's
# core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default, and set on the machine this repo is
# developed from — otherwise hands a fresh clone CRLF, leaving the working copy
# different from production for no reason anyone chose.
#
# This is HYGIENE, not a fix for a defect in this repo. An audit on 2026-08-04
# checked every file under test/ that reads real source:
#   test/negative-control-gate3.js PREPENDS its plant (PLANT_LINE + original).
#   There is no anchor to break.
# Nothing here is currently CRLF-fragile.
#
# The reason it is pinned anyway: the sibling platform Dragon-Ginseng-CS-AI lost
# 21 of 88 negative-control plants to CRLF, silently, and only found out on a
# fresh clone. Its harnesses match MULTI-LINE anchors, which is the fragile
# shape; this repo's do not. Pinning LF keeps that true if a future harness is
# written the other way, rather than relying on nobody writing one.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these, whatever they contain.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
